Magnesium is a mineral that helps turn the food we eat into energy and supports normal function of the parathyroid glands, as well as contributing to healthy bones, muscle development and nerve function (NHS, https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/vitamins-and-minerals/others; NHS, https://flipbooks.leedsth.nhs.uk/LN001144.pdf). It is found in foods such as spinach, nuts, wholemeal bread, wholegrain breakfast cereals, sardines, cheese and other items (NHS, https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/vitamins-and-minerals/others; NHS, https://flipbooks.leedsth.nhs.uk/LN001144.pdf). The recommended daily intake for adults is 300 mg for men and 270 mg for women aged 19‑64 (NHS, https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/vitamins-and-minerals/others).

